-- title:
--   Supersingular chart and its q+1 nodes at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, $M'$ is a positive integer with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (the rigid auxiliary-level guard).
--
--   **Place and reduction data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`). $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lying in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$. The hypothesis `hle` states that the base-changed full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,j$, $d \mid M'$) is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M')(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and with a degree-preserving map on places, satisfying the divisor-transport condition of that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s \in W$ is a distinguished supersingular place.
--
--   **Small-constants package.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$; writing $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the hypotheses require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime package.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (an element of $K_b$ lies in $A_b$ precisely when it lies in $A$), and $\varpi_b \ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ characterised by: $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$. Then there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (i) $W_0 \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$: for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (ii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (iii) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal.
--
--   (iv) (Specialisation at $s$.) For every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has no pole at any place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ has no pole, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (v) (Level stability.) For every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and every $f \in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in W_0$.
--
--   (vi) (Affine chart.) There are a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (a) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$;
--
--   (b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and conversely every element of that compositum is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (c) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (d) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$;
--
--   (e) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime, and $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation: an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$ in $B$;
--
--   (f) the image of $j$ lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under all the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (g) there is an element $b$ of $F_0$ lying in $B$ which lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ such that $V \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, $j$ lies in $V$, and $p(j)$ is a unit at $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$;
--
--   (h) for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is an element $b$ of $F_0$ lying in $B$ which lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$ that satisfies the analogue of (iv) for $s'$ (with $V$ in place of $W_0$);
--
--   (i) (Drinfeld special fibre.) For every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field of the $C_s$-action on the Drinfeld function field) such that: $\#C_s = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ (the width invariant $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ divided by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$); the kernel of $\rho$ is generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on constants from $A_b$ is reduction $A \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map into the quotient field; every element of the quotient field is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g, h \in B$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and $\rho$ is equivariant, in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f \in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f \in B$, the image of $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f)$ in the Drinfeld function field is obtained from that of $\rho(f)$ by $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$;
--
--   (j) (Nodes.) There is a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$ with exactly $q+1$ members such that:
--
--   • for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ with $f \in O \iff \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in O'$ for all $f \in F_0$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$;
--
--   • for every $\zeta$ and all $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising this correspondence between $O$ and $O'$ (the level action is transitive on the nodes);
--
--   • distinct $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ are separated: some $f \in F_0$ lies in both and is a non-unit of $O$ but a unit of $O'$;
--
--   • every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$ satisfying the analogue of (iv) for $s$ with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$) or is dominated by a node: there is $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ with $O \subseteq V$ such that every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   • and every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ satisfies: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $O \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$; every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ by a non-unit of $O$; and there exist an integer $E_0 \ge 1$ together with a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$ (both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\,v$, with $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$ (two-variable power series modulo $UV - \pi_0^{E_0}$), and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends constants from $A \cap k_0$ to the corresponding constants of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is a unit there; moreover
--
--   – there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_x$, $W_x \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t \in W_x$ such that any polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ whose value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ has all its coefficients in that maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ a unit there, and such that for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field with base change in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and with no pole where $j$ has none, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, should that residue lie in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs by a non-unit of $O$ from the image of every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$;
--
--   – and there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ such that every element of $B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every element of $B_x$ has no pole at any place of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ has no pole; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at those of its elements that are units in $O$ (an $f \in F_0$ lies in $O$ exactly when $f h = g$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$); every element of $F_0$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$, $h \ne 0$; $B_x$ is generated as a ring by the constants from $A \cap k_0$ together with a finite set $T$; and there is $b \in B_x$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, with $j \in V$ and $p(j)$ a unit at $V$ for all monic $A$-integral $p$ over $k_0$, provided some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, under the rigid auxiliary-level guard provided by a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ near a supersingular point: a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ specialising to the chosen supersingular place $s$, a formally smooth affine chart $B$ over the base whose special fibre is a quotient of the Drinfeld curve over the residue field, and the $q+1$ nodes on that chart, each with its crossing-model description $UV = \pi_0^{E_0}$ and its two branches. It is deduced from the corresponding statement carrying further conclusions (moduli Hasse invariant, common chart, Igusa separation and inertia data), and is used in the comparison of the node charts with the adic stalks of the normal model.
